{ Original Hippopotamus as Black course. Study material, not a historical game. } 1. e4 g6 2. d4 Bg7 3. Nc3 d6 4. Be3 a6 5. Qd2 b6 6. Nf3 Bb7 { Authored anchor. White prepares flexible castling and may seek Bh6 to exchange the g7 bishop. Black must notice the attacking setup before automatically playing ...h6. } 7. O-O-O Nf6 8. Bh6 Bxh6 9. Qxh6 Bxe4 10. Ng5 Bb7 { Plan: Compare ...e6 and ...Nd7 while choosing a safe king destination. If Bh6 is possible, decide whether to exchange, retreat or create central counterplay. Opponent resource: White can castle long and push h4. Removing the fianchetto bishop may weaken dark squares around a castled black king. } *

