{ Original Hippopotamus as Black course. Study material, not a historical game. } 1. d4 g6 2. c4 Bg7 3. Nf3 d6 4. g3 a6 5. Bg2 b6 6. O-O Bb7 7. Nc3 e6 { Authored anchor. Both sides have long-diagonal bishops, but White has more central space. The g2 bishop creates pressure against b7 when the center opens. } 8. e4 Nd7 9. Re1 h6 10. h4 Ne7 { Plan: Develop knights and prepare a break that releases your own bishops. Recount b7 and e4 pressure after each central pawn exchange. Opponent resource: White can advance d5 or e4 with good support. A quiet fianchetto can still produce a strong squeeze. } *

