{ Original Hippopotamus as Black course. Study material, not a historical game. } 1. d4 g6 2. Nf3 Bg7 3. e3 d6 4. Bd3 b6 5. O-O Bb7 6. Nbd2 e6 7. c3 Nd7 { Authored anchor. Without c4 White has less queenside space but a compact center. Black can develop flexibly and often challenge d4 with ...c5. } 8. e4 Ngf6 9. a4 O-O 10. b4 c5 { Plan: Decide whether the f8 knight belongs on e7 or f6. Prepare castling and use ...c5 when the resulting exchanges do not expose your king. Opponent resource: e4 can suddenly build a broad center and threaten e5. The modest e3 setup may be a preparation rather than a permanent concession. } *

