{ Original Hippopotamus as Black course. Study material, not a historical game. } 1. e4 g6 2. d4 Bg7 3. Nc3 d6 4. Nf3 e6 5. e5 dxe5 6. dxe5 Qxd1+ 7. Nxd1 { Authored anchor. Central exchanges can open the d-file and permit a queen trade. Black is no longer building a full Hippo and should value development and king activity accordingly. } 7... b6 8. Bb5+ Bd7 9. Be2 Bc6 10. Bf4 Nd7 { Plan: Develop the pieces toward active squares and target the advanced e5 pawn if possible. Do not continue irrelevant wing pawn moves after the position has opened. Opponent resource: White retains space and can develop quickly. Queenless positions still punish undeveloped pieces and weak pawns. } *

