{ Original Hippopotamus as Black course. Study material, not a historical game. } 1. e4 g6 2. d4 Bg7 3. c4 d6 4. Nc3 e6 5. Nf3 Ne7 6. Be2 O-O 7. O-O { Authored anchor. White occupies c4-d4-e4. Black chooses a partial formation and castles instead of insisting on both fianchettos before addressing the center. } 7... h6 8. Re1 b6 9. Be3 f5 10. exf5 Nxf5 { Plan: Prepare ...c5 or ...d5 with enough support. A bishop on b7 is useful only if its diagonal and the required tempi justify it. Opponent resource: White can gain more space with d5 or build a kingside attack with f4. Do not add ...a6 and ...h6 automatically under a development deficit. } *

