{ Original Hippopotamus as Black course. Study material, not a historical game. } 1. e4 g6 2. d4 Bg7 3. c4 d6 4. Nc3 e6 5. f4 Ne7 6. Nf3 O-O { Authored anchor. White adds f4 and may push e5 or f5. Black prioritizes development and king safety; a full Hippo is not the automatic answer. } 7. Be3 Nd7 8. Qd2 a6 9. Bf2 b6 10. Bd3 c5 { Plan: Challenge the center with ...c5 when ready, then calculate d5 and exchanges. Keep pieces aimed at the pawn chain rather than retreating without a plan. Opponent resource: White's attack may become dangerous if allowed to consolidate every pawn. You need a break, not merely a compact-looking position. } *

