{ Original Hippopotamus as Black course. Study material, not a historical game. } 1. e4 g6 2. d4 Bg7 3. Nc3 d6 4. h4 h5 { Authored anchor. ...h5 stops the immediate h4-h5 lever. Black accepts a fixed kingside structure rather than allowing White to open the h-file by force. } 5. Bg5 Nf6 6. Qd2 c6 7. a4 Nbd7 8. Be2 Qa5 9. Nf3 O-O 10. O-O Re8 { Plan: Develop while watching g4 and the central breaks. Keep the king flexible until you know whether the h-file will open. Opponent resource: g4 can attack the new h5 hook. A blocked h-pawn does not mean the king side is permanently safe. } *

