{ Original Hippopotamus as Black course. Study material, not a historical game. } 1. e4 g6 2. d4 Bg7 3. Nc3 d6 4. g4 { Authored anchor. White spends time on a wing attack before completing development. Black must calculate central action instead of reacting only on the attacked wing. } 4... Nc6 5. d5 Nd4 6. h3 e5 7. Nb1 c6 8. c3 Nb5 9. Be3 Nf6 10. Nd2 Nc7 { Plan: Examine ...c5 or ...h5, checking captures and king safety. Develop with threats when possible; the center is the natural place to test a premature wing expansion. Opponent resource: A careless ...h6 can provide the exact hook White wants. Do not complete a decorative pawn wall while the g-pawn advances. } *

