{ Original Hippopotamus as Black course. Study material, not a historical game. } 1. e4 g6 2. d4 Bg7 3. Nc3 d6 4. e5 dxe5 5. dxe5 Qxd1+ 6. Nxd1 Nc6 { Authored anchor. Black opens the center and trades queens, then develops with pressure on e5. The immediate central decision takes precedence over any plan to double fianchetto. } 7. f4 f6 8. Bb5 Bd7 9. exf6 Nxf6 10. Nf3 a6 { Plan: Develop actively and coordinate pieces against e5. Compare a useful capture with a developing move instead of trying to recreate the original pawn structure. Opponent resource: White can defend e5 and use the space advantage. A queen trade is a transition to a playable struggle, not proof that Black has won a pawn. } *

