{ Original Hippopotamus as Black course. Study material, not a historical game. } 1. b3 g6 2. Bb2 Nf6 3. e3 Bg7 4. Nf3 d6 5. d4 e6 { Authored anchor. The bishop on b2 already attacks g7 along an open diagonal. Black first develops Nf6 to block that line before placing an undefended bishop on g7. } 6. g3 b6 7. Bg2 Bb7 8. O-O O-O 9. c4 Nbd7 10. Qc2 c5 { Plan: Develop the queen side and choose a central break. This move order uses Nf6 instead of the standard Ne7 because a concrete threat determines the piece placement. Opponent resource: Playing ...Bg7 immediately after Bb2 would simply leave that bishop en prise. A normal-looking fianchetto is not safe in every move order. } *

