{ Original Hippopotamus as Black course. Study material, not a historical game. } 1. e4 g6 2. d4 Bg7 3. Nc3 d6 4. Nf3 e6 5. Be2 Ne7 6. O-O O-O 7. Be3 Nd7 { Authored anchor. Black develops the queen knight before forcing a central break. In this exact position an immediate ...c5 allows strong white play; a thematic move still needs preparation. } 8. Qd2 a6 9. a4 b6 10. Rfe1 Bb7 { Plan: Compare ...c5 and ...d5 on the next move after checking White's reply. If ...c5 becomes safe, calculate dxc5 and d5 separately and identify the opened file. Opponent resource: White can improve with Qd2 or advance in the center. Do not assume that a break becomes good simply because it belongs to the opening's vocabulary. } *

