{ Original Hippopotamus as Black course. Study material, not a historical game. } 1. e4 g6 2. d4 Bg7 3. Nc3 d6 4. Nf3 e6 5. Be2 Ne7 6. O-O O-O 7. Be3 d5 { Authored anchor. ...d5 directly challenges e4 but creates a new pawn contact and can be captured. Black chooses activity instead of preserving the original d6-e6 shell. } 8. Re1 dxe4 9. Nxe4 b6 10. h4 Bb7 { Plan: Compare exd5 and e5, including the effect on the bishops. Reposition pieces toward the opened files instead of clinging to their original squares. Opponent resource: A premature ...d5 can leave a weak isolated pawn or open lines before development is ready. Calculate all forcing replies. } *

