{ Original Hippopotamus as Black course. Study material, not a historical game. } 1. e4 g6 2. d4 Bg7 3. Nc3 d6 4. Nf3 e6 5. d5 e5 { Authored anchor. Black meets d5 with ...e5 and closes the center. This gives a clear pawn-chain structure but also restricts the g7 bishop. } 6. Be2 Ne7 7. Be3 Nd7 8. g4 Nf6 9. h3 O-O 10. Qd2 a6 { Plan: Consider a later ...f5 after preparation or queenside play with ...c6. Choose the wing based on the pawn chain and king safety. Opponent resource: White can expand with c4 and b4 or attack on the king side. A blocked center gives maneuvering time, not unlimited time. } *

