{ Original Hippopotamus as Black course. Study material, not a historical game. } 1. e4 g6 2. d4 Bg7 3. Nc3 d6 4. Nf3 e6 5. e5 dxe5 6. dxe5 Qxd1+ 7. Nxd1 { Authored anchor. Black exchanges the advanced pawn and uses the open d-file to trade queens. In this exact move order, blocking with ...d5 gives White a stronger bind and attacking chances. } 7... Bd7 8. Nc3 a6 9. Bd3 Bc6 10. Be4 h6 { Plan: Develop actively and challenge e5 with pieces. King activity and pawn targets now matter more than recreating the full Hippo formation. Opponent resource: White retains space and can consolidate the advanced pawn. A queen trade changes the type of struggle rather than ending it. } *

